# DEBUG-ONLY, one-shot bench fragment -- DISPLAY_ST7796_PLAN.md Sec.4 /
# Sec.12 Phase 4. Not applied by default: sdkconfig.defaults does not
# reference this file, so a normal `idf.py build` never picks it up.
#
# Selects CONFIG_KILNCTL_DISPLAY_PANEL_AUTO instead of the shipped
# CONFIG_KILNCTL_DISPLAY_PANEL_ILI9488 default. This is the ONLY way to make
# ILI9488_start() (panel_spi.c) actually call ILI9488_read_id() at boot --
# the explicit-ILI9488 branch never reads RDDID at all (see the corrected
# TODO comment in panel_detect.h). AUTO's own bootstrap panel is ILI9488, so
# this needs no wiring change to read the currently-attached ILI9488's ID;
# to read the ST7796's ID instead, wire the MSP4031 to J2 (only after the
# STOP-block 5V hazard check in the plan) and use
# CONFIG_KILNCTL_DISPLAY_PANEL_ST7796 directly, not this file.
#
# One-time procedure:
#   1. idf.py -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.paneldetect.defaults" build
#   2. flash_firmware() (or the usual OpenOCD flash path), then read the
#      boot log for the "panel auto-detect: no RDDID match (read 0x.. 0x..
#      0x.. ...)" WARN from panel_spi.c -- an all-0x00/all-0xFF read means
#      MISO is not driven, not a real ID (see ILI9488_read_id()'s comment).
#   3. Record the three bytes in DISPLAY_ST7796_PLAN.md Sec.4, then rebuild
#      WITHOUT this fragment (plain `idf.py build`) before flashing again --
#      AUTO is a detection tool, not the shipped configuration, and this
#      file must never be added to sdkconfig.defaults itself.
#
# This changes only which panel_desc_t boots and whether RDDID gets read; it
# does not touch SPI timing, CS behaviour, or the MAX31856 thermocouple
# path -- ILI9488_read_id() goes through the same spi_owner_transfer()
# arbitration every other display SPI transaction already uses.
CONFIG_KILNCTL_DISPLAY_PANEL_AUTO=y
